window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_main-3c90c9d469127b25"]={"key":"ny_main-3c90c9d469127b25","group":"ny_main","uid":"3c90c9d469127b25","rank":5,"title":"bellwether closing cash control procedure","occupation":"retail_sales_supervisors","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_main","prompt":"You’re the retail floor supervisor at Bellwether Cooperative, and Orla Yamamoto needs a closing and cash-control procedure ready for approval before Friday, ahead of Quillhaven Services taking over evening security next Monday. Write it for a newly authorised Bellwether closing supervisor facing their first unsupervised close, while keeping the approval points visible to Orla. The stocktake review completed this week covers the most recent five closing days: gross absolute till variance was £214 across nine till-level variance events, the largest single variance was £74, and seven inventory shrink adjustments totalling £189 carried comments referring to cash or till differences. Across the preceding four weeks, covering 20 closing days, gross absolute till variance was £96 across six events, the largest was £28, and three shrink adjustments totalling £41 carried comparable comments. We do not have transaction counts, sales values, till-user hours, or evidence identifying the cause, so do not invent them or attribute the pattern to an individual, the security change, or misconduct. Two Bellwether-authorised people are normally required for the final cash count, and Quillhaven officers are not authorised to count, handle, approve, or take custody of Bellwether cash. The staffing roster can nevertheless leave only one authorised closer by the time lockup is due. England locations have a Quillhaven lockup window ending at 22:15, while Scotland locations end at 22:00; local emergency instructions, assembly points, and contact routes also vary by site. Staff commonly say to keep recounting until a drawer balances, but in this setting repeated recounts can run beyond the security window and leave one person inside after lockup. There is also a rare but severe closing risk involving suspected forced entry, a threatening person, or coercion, which is too serious to bury inside ordinary variance guidance. Produce one presentation-ready procedure that (1) compares the two review periods on a like-for-like basis and explains what is materially different without claiming a cause; (2) gives a new closing supervisor an operable normal-close path from the end of trading through recorded handover; (3) gives the lone-authorised-closer case its own bounded path without quietly weakening either the two-person rule or the lockup control; (4) makes the limit of the repeated-recount rule of thumb unambiguous; (5) distinguishes the severe safety exception from routine discrepancies and ordinary lone closing; (6) actively warns against using an inventory shrink adjustment, stock write-off, sale, refund, or similar entry to clear a cash difference; (7) compares applicability for England and Scotland so neither lockup window nor local emergency information is treated as universal; and (8) clearly labels every operating threshold, contact route, retention period, or other company-specific detail that is not supplied here as an assumption requiring approval rather than established Bellwether policy. Orla must be able to identify the bounded decision she is approving for lone-closer shifts and the control consequences, but you are not authorised to recommend a staffing increase, a Quillhaven contract change, disciplinary action, or any other management action. Keep till-system click paths, opening procedures, bank-deposit transport, and disciplinary investigation out of scope. The procedure must be editable, practical at the point of closing, and no more than four pages total with no appendices. Write the finished file into the top level of your working directory using exactly the filename `bellwether_closing_cash_control_procedure.docx`.\n\n---\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `bellwether_closing_cash_control_procedure.docx` — Presentation-ready operating procedure for normal closing, cash variances, lone-authorised-closer conditions, jurisdictional applicability, and the severe safety exception. (Place the file at the top level of the working directory using the exact filename.; The document must be editable and render correctly as a DOCX.; Maximum four pages total, with no appendices.; Write for a newly authorised Bellwether closing supervisor on their first unsupervised close.; Use only the supplied operating figures and clearly label unsupported company-specific details as assumptions for approval.; Do not include till-system click paths, opening procedures, bank-deposit transport, disciplinary investigation, staffing recommendations, or security-contract recommendations.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/bellwether_closing_cash_control_procedure.docx","bytes":46773,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/a79f7a346b65e6f9bbef3567a6c0ade7e8a156584445ba644335ae7e6012cfd4.docx","sha256":"a79f7a346b65e6f9bbef3567a6c0ade7e8a156584445ba644335ae7e6012cfd4","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"CLOSING & CASH-CONTROL\nPROCEDURE\n \nDOCUMENT OWNER\nRetail Floor Supervision\nVERSION / PREPARED\n0.9 / 16 August 2026\nPRIMARY USER\nNewly authorised closing supervisor\nAPPROVAL STATUS\nDRAFT - Orla Yamamoto decision required\nIssue status: not approved or issued. Use after approval only.\nAPPROVAL DECISION REQUESTED - ORLA YAMAMOTO\nDRAFT DECISION: where only one Bellwether-authorised closer remains and a second cannot complete a final count before the applicable Quillhaven lockup-window end, permit controlled deferral only: preserve till evidence, seal and restrict the funds, record DEFERRED, complete safe lockup, and assign the next authorised pair to complete. This is not permission for a solo final count or Quillhaven substitution. Consequence: reconciliation remains deliberately incomplete overnight; no two-person count attestation is made, while the two-person rule and lockup control remain intact.\n\nPurpose, use and boundaries\nUse at every Bellwether close from end of trading through recorded cash handover. It is for a newly authorised closing supervisor when a close begins, a till differs, only one authorised closer may remain, or a severe safety event arises. Out of scope: opening, till-system click paths, bank-deposit transport, disciplinary investigation, staffing recommendations and Quillhaven contract recommendations.\nTwo authorised people\nA normal final count needs two Bellwether cash-authorised people: one counter and one independent verifier. Mere building presence is not a cash-control role.\nQuillhaven boundary\nQuillhaven officers provide physical security, access/lockup support and incident response only. They never count, handle, approve, attest to, or take custody of Bellwether cash or stock adjustments.\nNo artificial balancing\nA cash difference stays in the cash-variance record. Never use a shrink adjustment, stock write-off, sale, refund or similar entry to make a till appear to balance.\nReview basis - like-for-like closing-day comparison\nMeasure\nPreceding four weeks\n(20 closes)\nMost recent five days\n(5 closes)\nChange / reading\nGross absolute till variance\n£96\n£4.80 per close\n£214\n£42.80 per close\n+£38.00 per close\n+791.7%\nTill-level variance events\n6\n0.30 per close\n9\n1.80 per close\n+1.50 per close\n+500.0%\nLargest single variance\n£28\n£74\n+£46\n+164.3%\nCash/till-referenced shrink comments\n3 adjustments\n£41\n7 adjustments\n£189\n+4 adjustments\n+£148\nReading: the five-day period is materially worse after allowing for its shorter duration: gross absolute till variance is £42.80 per close versus £4.80, and events are 1.80 versus 0.30 per close. Cash/till wording in stock-adjustment comments is a control warning, not proof of cause. No transaction volumes, sales values, till-user hours, causal evidence or individual evidence were supplied; do not attribute this pattern to a person, the Quillhaven transition or misconduct.\nEngland and Scotland applicability\nThe supplied windows are operating requirements, not statements of law. Common cash controls above apply in both locations.\nApplies to\nLockup operating requirement\nLocal information\nEngland\nQuillhaven lockup window ends at 22:15. Treat it as the supplied operating deadline, not a statutory requirement.\nUse the England site’s current emergency instructions, assembly point and contact route. Do not assume another site’s details apply.\nScotland\nQuillhaven lockup window ends at 22:00. Treat it as the supplied operating deadline, not a statutory requirement.\nUse the Scotland site’s current emergency instructions, assembly point and contact route. Do not assume another site’s details apply.\n\n\nAt the close: choose the path\nSAFETY FIRST\nSuspected forced entry, threatening person or coercion? Stop normal work and go to the Severe Safety Exception on page 4. It overrides counting, variance and lone-close steps.\nSTAFFING AND TIME CHECK\nAt the start of closing preparations, identify the site (England 22:15 / Scotland 22:00), confirm the current local emergency plan, and confirm whether two Bellwether-authorised people can complete before the applicable window. If not, use page 3 immediately.\nDo not discover a one-person conflict at final count. A Quillhaven officer may support access, exit and lockup only; their building presence cannot satisfy the second Bellwether cash-control role.\nPath A - normal close with two authorised Bellwether people\n1\nEnd trading; control access\nComplete the established end-of-trading stage. Restrict the count area to the authorised counter and independent verifier; do not expose cash to other staff or Quillhaven. Keep every till separately identified from the outset.\n2\nCapture and original count\nFor one till at a time, preserve the till identifier and original expected balance/till report. The counter records the original actual amount and time. Do not pool cash or offset one till against another.\n3\nIndependent verification\nThe verifier independently checks the same till as the single controlled recount. Compare to expected and resolve transcription, denomination or till-identity errors without overwriting the original count. Both authorised people attest only to a completed count result.\n4\nStop and record a difference\nNever keep recounting until a drawer balances. DRAFT APPROVAL ASSUMPTION: one independent controlled recount per till is the maximum. If still unexplained, preserve both results, record the over/short and escalate; safety and the lockup window always stop further recounting.\n5\nProtect cash and evidence\nUse controlled tamper-evident packaging; record its unique package/seal ID, time, site and linked till(s), count status and report reference. Put it in approved secure storage with restricted access. Packaging and storage method/access list require local approval confirmation.\n6\nRecorded handover and lockup\nEvery custody transfer is between authorised Bellwether roles and records transfer, receipt and package/seal identity. If integrity is not confirmed, record and escalate it. Give Quillhaven only physical-security status, confirm people have exited or are covered by the site plan, secure access points and finish lockup by the applicable window.\nRECOUNT RULE - UNAMBIGUOUS STOP\nThe verifier's single independent check is the controlled recount. It does not become an open-ended search for a balancing figure. An unresolved difference is a recorded cash variance and is escalated; it is never a reason to delay safe lockup or leave one person inside after the window.\n\n\n\nPath B - one authorised closer: controlled deferral, never a solo final count\nTRIGGER AND BOUNDARY\nUse this path as soon as it is clear that only one Bellwether-authorised person will remain for final count, or a second cannot complete the count safely before the England 22:15 or Scotland 22:00 lockup-window end. This is a staffing/time control conflict, not an ordinary variance and not the severe safety exception.\n\n1\nEscalate early\nRecord the applicable window and immediately use the current approved site cash-control / management escalation route before that end time. CONTACT ROUTE AND RESPONSE OWNER ARE DRAFT APPROVAL ASSUMPTIONS; no Bellwether route was supplied. If a second Bellwether-authorised person can complete the count before lockup, return to Path A.\n2\nHold the hard controls\nIf no second authorised person can join in time, do not perform a solo final count, do not use a Quillhaven officer as counter, verifier, custodian or approver, and do not stay unsecured after the window. Quillhaven may coordinate physical security only.\n3\nPlace cash in a deferred state\nDo not declare reconciliation complete. Preserve each till's identity and original till report/expected balance. Record whether it is uncounted or incompletely counted. Seal till funds and records in controlled tamper-evident packaging; record date/time, site, till(s), unique seal/package ID, reason and status: DEFERRED - NO TWO-PERSON FINAL COUNT.\n4\nRestrict custody; lock up safely\nThe lone closer attests only to packaging, secure-storage placement and deferred status - never to a final count. Store under restricted authorised access in the approved local secure-cash location (location/access list require approval confirmation). Complete exit and secured-access checks with Quillhaven by the applicable window; disclose no cash amounts, variance details or package IDs.\nClose the deferral with the next authorised pair\nA\nDocumented receipt\nThe next available pair of Bellwether-authorised people receives the deferred package through a documented transfer/receipt. Match the site, till link, time and package/seal ID to the deferred record before opening. No exact completion time is supplied; any deadline must be approved as an assumption.\nB\nIntegrity before count\nVerify seal/package integrity. If it is broken, missing or mismatched, record an integrity discrepancy, preserve the evidence and escalate through the approved route; do not sign it off as intact or quietly treat it as a routine completed deferral.\nC\nTwo-person completion\nCounter and verifier complete Path A, compare to the preserved expected balance/till report and any partial result, record each variance by till, and both attest to completion. Cross-reference the deferred record and close the custody trail without erasing the original state.\nSECURITY HANDOVER LANGUAGE\nCommunicate status sufficient for physical lockup, for example that the close is ready or deferred and people are exiting. Confirm staff have exited or are otherwise covered by the local site plan, then secure access points within the site window.\nDO NOT DISCLOSE OR TRANSFER\nDo not give Quillhaven cash totals, variance values, till identities, package/seal identifiers or custody. An officer can record their own security observation but cannot attest to a Bellwether cash record.\n\n\nSevere safety exception - suspected forced entry, threat or coercion\nLIFE SAFETY OVERRIDES THE NORMAL AND LONE-CLOSE PATHS\nStop the count and stop handling cash. Do not confront, challenge, pursue, detain, re-enter, attempt evidence recovery or protect cash ahead of people. Follow the current site-specific emergency instructions, assembly point and contact route; contact emergency services when safe. Quillhaven's role remains physical security and incident support under the site plan, never cash control. Only after immediate danger has passed: preserve records or the scene without disturbing it where safe, restrict unnecessary access, record factual observations and notify through the approved local route. Do not resume reconciliation until the applicable local response permits it.\n\nRequired records and cash integrity\nCash variance record: capture all\n- date and time; site; till identifier\n- expected amount and actual amount; over or short direction\n- original count and controlled recount result; any transcription resolution\n- counter, verifier and other authorised participants\n- circumstances and evidence references (for example, till report or package/seal ID)\n- escalation route, recipient and disposition; deferred or completed status\nCustody and handover record: capture all\n- package or seal unique identifier; date/time; site and every linked till\n- package status, count status and accompanying till report reference\n- secure-storage location reference and restricted authorised access record\n- each transfer and receipt: sending and receiving authorised Bellwether roles and attestation\n- seal/package integrity check; record and escalate broken, missing or mismatched identity\n- completion record cross-referenced to any deferred cash record\nNever force a balance: do not net overages and shortages across drawers, shifts or days; transfer cash between tills; use personal reimbursement or IOUs; add or remove cash without record; delete evidence; backdate; or split a variance to avoid escalation.\nCash variance is not a stock transaction\nKEEP THE RECORDS SEPARATE\nA cash difference remains in the cash-variance record. Never use an inventory shrink adjustment, stock write-off, sale, refund or similar entry to clear it. A valid stock adjustment concerns a supported stock discrepancy and needs item, quantity, reason, evidence and appropriate stock approval.\nREVIEW PRIOR CASH-REFERENCED SHRINK ENTRIES\nDo not assume every prior entry is wrong and do not delete its audit trail. Review traceably. If evidence supports correction, the appropriate stock approver makes an authorised reversal or correcting entry that preserves the original record and cross-references the underlying cash variance.\nRoutine variance escalation and approval assumptions\nFor an unresolved cash variance or custody-integrity discrepancy, preserve records/evidence and report facts through the current approved cash-control or management route. Limit access to need-to-know people. The supervisor makes no accusation or disciplinary finding. No monetary threshold is set by this draft; any threshold requires approval.\nDRAFT ASSUMPTIONS REQUIRING APPROVAL BEFORE ISSUE: one controlled verifier recount per till; escalation contact route/owner; packaging, secure-storage and access-record method; local emergency/assembly/contact references; method of attestation; record-retention period; and any deadline for deferred-count completion. None is established Bellwether policy in this brief.\nORLA YAMAMOTO - REVIEW DECISION\n[ ] Approve draft  [ ] Amend  [ ] Do not approve\nSignature / date: ______________________________\nBEFORE ISSUE\nConfirm local site emergency information, England/Scotland window, secure storage/access reference and approved escalation route.\nComments: ______________________________________","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The required DOCX exists under the exact filename, opens without repair warnings, and contains editable document content rather than only a flattened image.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Submitted filename, DOCX package integrity, and editable body content.","grader_hint":"Open the file and inspect its package and body. Award only if the exact filename is used and the content is editable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The complete procedure renders within four pages, with no appendix or other overflow used to evade the cap.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Rendered page count and all document sections.","grader_hint":"Render the DOCX using a standard office renderer and count every page, including approval or reference pages."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document is identifiable as a controlled draft for approval and provides practical ownership, version or revision, date, and approval-status information without pretending approval has already occurred.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Document-control information and approval language.","grader_hint":"Accept any concise professional document-control treatment. Do not require a particular table or field order."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The purpose, primary reader, trigger, and boundaries are clear: it governs closing and cash variance control, not opening, system click-throughs, deposit transport, disciplinary investigation, staffing recommendations, or contract recommendations.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Purpose, audience, scope, and exclusions.","grader_hint":"Check that a first-time closing supervisor can tell when to use the procedure and that excluded processes are not developed into substantive instructions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The period comparison normalizes gross absolute till variance by closing days: £96 divided by 20 equals £4.80 per close and £214 divided by 5 equals £42.80 per close, each within ±£0.01; any stated change equals £38.00 per close within ±£0.01 or 791.7% within ±0.1 percentage points.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Period-comparison calculations in the document.","grader_hint":"Recalculate from the stated totals and closing-day counts. Gross absolute variance must not be treated as a signed net balance."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The comparison normalizes variance-event frequency: six events over 20 closes equals 0.30 per close and nine events over five closes equals 1.80 per close, each within ±0.01 event per close.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Variance-event comparison.","grader_hint":"Accept an equivalent expression such as one event per 3.33 closes versus 1.8 events per close if mathematically consistent within ±1%."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The largest single variance is correctly compared as £28 versus £74, with an increase of £46 within ±£1 or 164.3% within ±0.1 percentage points.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Largest-variance comparison.","grader_hint":"Award if both source amounts and at least one correct change measure are clear."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The cash-referenced shrink-adjustment comparison reports three adjustments totalling £41 versus seven totalling £189 and correctly derives four additional flagged adjustments and a £148 increase within ±£1.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Comparison of flagged adjustment counts and values.","grader_hint":"Check both count and amount relationships. The document may call these flagged or cash-referenced entries but must not present them as proven fraud."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The narrative explains that the current period is materially worse even after allowing for its shorter duration, while distinguishing observed association from an established cause.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Interpretive text accompanying the period comparison.","grader_hint":"Look for a meaningful interpretation of the normalized pattern. Reject causal claims about named people, the security transition, or misconduct that the figures do not establish."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Material data limitations and approval assumptions are conspicuous, including the absence of transaction volume, sales value, till-user-hour, causal, and internal-threshold evidence.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Assumptions, limitations, and approval markers throughout the procedure.","grader_hint":"Company-specific thresholds, contacts, and retention periods may be proposed only when clearly labelled as draft assumptions or approval blanks."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The procedure clearly associates England with a 22:15 lockup-window end and Scotland with a 22:00 lockup-window end.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Jurisdiction applicability text or table.","grader_hint":"Search for both jurisdiction names and times, then confirm each time is attached to the correct jurisdiction and treated as a deadline rather than a suggested target."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The England/Scotland comparison separates common Bellwether cash controls from jurisdiction- or site-specific lockup and emergency information and does not mislabel contractual times as statutory requirements.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Applicability and jurisdiction language.","grader_hint":"Check that the document directs users to the applicable local emergency instructions and does not invent legal differences or universal contact details."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The normal-close path has an executable sequence covering the end of trading, restriction of access to the counting area, till or cash capture, verification, discrepancy handling, secure storage, records, and handover.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Normal-close operating sequence.","grader_hint":"Evaluate operational completeness rather than requiring particular headings. The sequence must be usable without inventing missing steps at the counter."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Each till remains separately accountable through reconciliation, with overages and shortages recorded by till and not netted across drawers, shifts, or days.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Till-level reconciliation and recording rules.","grader_hint":"Look for explicit preservation of till identity and a prohibition on offsetting one variance against another."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The normal final count requires two Bellwether-authorised people and assigns counter and verifier responsibilities without treating mere building presence as the second cash-control role.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Roles in the two-person count.","grader_hint":"Confirm that both participants are cash-authorised Bellwether personnel and that one has a genuine verification duty."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The verification control preserves the original count, provides an independent check or recount, resolves transcription differences, and requires both authorised participants to attest to the result.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Counting and verification instructions and required records.","grader_hint":"Accept signatures, initials, or authenticated electronic attestations. The second person must do more than watch passively."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The procedure sets a finite recount boundary and a clear stop condition, so an unexplained difference is recorded and escalated rather than repeatedly recounted until it appears to balance or the lockup control is breached.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Recount and stop-condition instructions.","grader_hint":"A single controlled recount is a strong solution, but accept another finite, defensible limit if any unsupported company rule is labelled for approval and safety and lockup remain controlling constraints."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The procedure prohibits artificial cash balancing through transfers between tills, personal reimbursement or IOUs, undocumented cash removal or addition, deletion of evidence, backdating, or splitting a variance to avoid escalation.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Cash-integrity warnings and discrepancy rules.","grader_hint":"Equivalent plain-language prohibitions are acceptable. This item does not require disciplinary content."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The variance record captures enough information for later review: date and time, site and till identifier, expected and actual amounts, over or short direction, original and recount results, participants, circumstances, evidence references, and escalation or disposition.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Required variance-record fields.","grader_hint":"The fields may appear in prose, a checklist, or a reusable form. Award when the resulting record supports reconstruction and accountability."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Cash awaiting completion or handover is protected with controlled packaging or a tamper-evident seal, a unique identifier, time and till linkage, secure storage, and restricted access.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Cash-securing and chain-of-custody instructions.","grader_hint":"Do not require a particular brand or system. The control must make later interference detectable and associate the package with its records."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Every custody handoff requires documented transfer and receipt by authorised roles, including seal or package identity and discrepancy escalation if integrity is not confirmed.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Handover and custody-record requirements.","grader_hint":"Check that custody does not pass informally and that a broken, missing, or mismatched seal triggers escalation rather than routine counting."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The procedure explains that inventory shrink adjustments belong only to supported stock discrepancies, with item, quantity, reason, evidence, and appropriate stock approval, while cash differences remain in the cash-variance record.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Stock-adjustment boundary and cash-variance treatment.","grader_hint":"Look for an affirmative explanation of the two separate accounting trails, not merely the absence of incorrect instructions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Previously posted cash-referenced shrink entries are handled through a traceable review and authorised reversal or correcting entry, with cross-reference to the underlying cash variance; the original audit trail is not erased.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Correction treatment for prior suspect adjustments.","grader_hint":"The document need not provide system clicks or decide that every flagged entry is wrong. It must preserve the original record and require evidence-based correction."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The lone-authorised-closer path starts with an early staffing and time check and requires escalation before the applicable security deadline, rather than discovering the conflict only at final count.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Lone-closer trigger and pre-close control.","grader_hint":"Look for a practical decision point tied to the remaining authorised staff and jurisdictional lockup window."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The lone-closer path does not allow a solo final count, does not substitute a Quillhaven officer for an authorised Bellwether counter or verifier, and does not solve the conflict by remaining unsecured after the lockup window.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Lone-closer restrictions.","grader_hint":"All three control boundaries must be maintained. An alternative approved Bellwether-authorised closer may participate if the procedure can still meet the lockup requirement."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"When a compliant two-person count cannot occur, the procedure provides a controlled deferral that secures the uncounted or incompletely counted funds, records the reason and status, preserves the till report and seal identity, and completes lockup safely.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Controlled-deferral instructions.","grader_hint":"The deferred state must be visibly different from a completed reconciliation and must not imply that the lone closer attested to a two-person count."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Deferred cash is assigned to the next authorised pair through a documented handoff, seal-integrity check, count, variance comparison, and completion record, with any exact completion deadline clearly marked as an approval assumption if used.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Deferred-count completion and accountability.","grader_hint":"Check that deferral is closed out rather than left indefinite and that the later pair can distinguish pre-existing variance from custody interference."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Security handover and lockup are integrated into the operating path, including timely status communication, confirmation that people have exited or are otherwise covered by the site plan, secured access points, and no disclosure of unnecessary cash details.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Quillhaven coordination and lockup instructions.","grader_hint":"The procedure should coordinate cash control with physical security without transferring cash authority to the security provider."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Quillhaven’s role is bounded to physical security, access or lockup support, and incident response; it is not assigned cash counting, cash custody, discrepancy approval, stock adjustment approval, or cash-record attestation.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Role definitions and handoff instructions.","grader_hint":"A security officer may document their own security observations but must not be represented as satisfying a Bellwether cash-control role."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Suspected forced entry, threat, or coercion has a visibly distinct emergency path and is not presented as an ordinary cash variance, generic lone-close variation, or reason to continue counting.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Separate severe-exception treatment.","grader_hint":"The rare event must be easy to locate under pressure and must clearly override routine cash and lockup steps where life safety requires it."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The severe-exception path prioritizes personal safety, no confrontation or evidence recovery attempt, stopping the count, following the applicable site emergency instructions, contacting emergency services when safe, and preserving records or the scene only after immediate danger has passed.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Actions under the forced-entry, threat, or coercion exception.","grader_hint":"Reject instructions that ask staff to challenge a person, protect cash before people, re-enter, detain anyone, or continue reconciliation during the threat."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Routine unexplained variances are escalated through functional management or cash-control roles with records and evidence preserved, access limited to need-to-know personnel, and no accusation or disciplinary finding made by the closing supervisor.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Routine escalation and confidentiality instructions.","grader_hint":"Accept role labels rather than invented names. Any monetary escalation threshold must be explicitly marked for approval because none was supplied."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The approval treatment presents a bounded lone-closer decision, its control consequences, and unresolved assumptions neutrally, clearly separating what Orla must approve from settled operating controls and avoiding a staffing or contract recommendation.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Approval panel, decision statement, or equivalent approval content.","grader_hint":"The senior reviewer should be able to identify the approval choice without reading the entire procedure. The document may state consequences but must not advocate a management action."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"A newly authorised closing supervisor can navigate the document at the point of work, identify the applicable path, understand who acts and when, complete the required records, and finish or defer the close without asking the author a procedural question.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Whole-document usability, action wording, navigation, and reusable operating aids.","grader_hint":"Judge the rendered artifact as an operating tool. Dense narrative that contains the facts but cannot be followed during closing should not receive full credit."},{"rubric_item_id":"R35","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Figures, role labels, deadlines, exception triggers, approval assumptions, and control states agree throughout the document, with no conflict between the normal, lone-closer, jurisdictional, and severe-exception paths.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Cross-section consistency within the submitted procedure.","grader_hint":"Trace at least one normal close, one England lone close, one Scotland lone close, and the severe exception. Check that each reaches a coherent end state."},{"rubric_item_id":"P01","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The procedure explicitly directs or permits an inventory shrink adjustment, stock write-off, sale, refund, or similar inventory transaction to force a cash difference to balance.","weight":-10.0,"polarity":"penalty","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Any instruction, example, decision path, or approval language authorising a non-cash entry as the balancing mechanism for a cash variance.","grader_hint":"Apply only for an affirmative authorisation or workaround, not merely because the warning is brief. Legitimate evidence-based stock corrections kept separate from cash variance handling do not trigger the penalty."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"Bellwether Cooperative is introducing a new evening security provider while unexplained till variances and cash-referenced stock adjustments are increasing. The procedure will be used by newly authorised closing supervisors and reviewed by a senior decision maker before approval.","difficulty_sources":["Reconciling the two-person cash-count rule with a hard security lockup when only one authorised closer remains","Normalizing unequal review periods and explaining a material deterioration without overstating causation","Separating cash-accountability records from inventory shrink corrections despite prior misuse","Defining where repeated recounting must stop without inventing unsupported company policy","Maintaining jurisdiction-specific lockup and emergency applicability while keeping common controls coherent","Giving a rare threat or coercion event a distinct life-safety path","Framing a bounded approval decision neutrally within the supervisor's limited authority"],"authoring_plan":{"reference_material":{"files_to_create":[],"instruction":"Do not create reference files. All fixed facts are in the request; the remaining substance comes from occupational cash-control and retail closing knowledge."},"solver_instance":"Produce an editable, presentation-ready closing procedure for a newly authorised retail closing supervisor, while exposing bounded approval assumptions to a senior reviewer. The procedure must reconcile cash accountability, stock-adjustment integrity, lone-working safety, and a hard security lockup without weakening one control to satisfy another.","period_relationships":{"gross_absolute_variance":"Baseline rate is 96/20 = £4.80 per close. Current rate is 214/5 = £42.80 per close. The rate increase is £38.00 per close and (42.80/4.80 - 1) × 100 = 791.6667%. The unnormalized total increase is £118 or 122.9167%, but the gold must explain why unequal period lengths make the per-close view more informative.","event_frequency":"Baseline event rate is 6/20 = 0.30 per close. Current event rate is 9/5 = 1.80 per close, an increase of 1.50 events per close or 500%.","largest_variance":"The largest single variance rises from £28 to £74, a £46 increase or (74/28 - 1) × 100 = 164.2857%.","cash_referenced_stock_adjustments":"Flagged adjustment count rises from three to seven, an increase of four. Flagged value rises from £41 to £189, an increase of £148. Treat comments as a control warning, not proof that every entry was improper.","interpretive_limit":"The gold must describe the pattern as materially worse after normalization while stating that missing sales, transaction, staffing-hour, till-user, and causal evidence prevents attribution."},"required_operating_behavior":{"normal_close":["End trading and control access before exposing or counting cash.","Keep each till separately identifiable and preserve the original expected balance or till report.","Use two cash-authorised retailer personnel, with one counting and the other independently verifying or recounting and both attesting.","Set a finite recount boundary; preserve the original result and record an unresolved variance rather than repeatedly recounting.","Do not net tills or days, borrow cash, use personal funds, alter records, backdate, delete evidence, or split discrepancies.","Record sufficient identifiers, amounts, participants, timestamps, recount outcome, evidence, and escalation details.","Seal and secure cash with identifiable custody records and document every authorised handoff."],"stock_adjustment_boundary":["A cash discrepancy remains a cash discrepancy and must not be cleared with an inventory, sale, refund, or stock-loss transaction.","A legitimate inventory adjustment requires stock-specific evidence such as item, quantity, reason, and appropriate inventory approval.","Previously flagged entries are reviewed rather than presumed fraudulent; an improper entry is corrected by an authorised reversal or correcting entry that preserves and cross-references the audit trail."],"lone_authorised_closer":["Detect the staffing conflict before the jurisdictional lockup deadline and escalate early.","Do not permit a solo final count and do not use security-provider personnel as cash counters, verifiers, custodians, or approvers.","If a second authorised retailer employee cannot participate within the lockup control, place the funds into a clearly recorded deferred state using tamper-evident packaging, till linkage, seal identity, time, reason, secure storage, and restricted access.","Complete lockup safely rather than remaining unsecured or extending repeated recounts.","Assign deferred completion to the next authorised pair, who verify package integrity, perform the count, reconcile to preserved records, record any variance, and close the custody trail.","Any exact completion deadline, escalation threshold, contact route, or retention term not provided must be marked for approval."],"security_interface":["Treat the supplied England and Scotland lockup windows as operating requirements, not statutes.","Keep security-provider duties to physical security, access and lockup support, and incident response.","Coordinate status and exit without disclosing unnecessary cash details or transferring cash authority."],"severe_exception":["Give suspected forced entry, threatening conduct, or coercion a separate and prominent path.","Life safety overrides counting and ordinary lockup sequencing: stop the count, do not confront or attempt evidence recovery, use local emergency instructions, contact emergency services when safe, and preserve records or the scene only after immediate danger passes.","Do not fold this event into the routine variance, lone-closer, or generic incident path."],"approval_boundary":["Clearly distinguish settled controls from the bounded lone-closer treatment and unsupported local details that require senior approval.","Present control consequences neutrally and do not recommend added staffing, a security-contract change, disciplinary action, or another management action."]},"must_not_assert":["Do not assert that the security transition, a named individual, theft, fraud, or misconduct caused the observed figures.","Do not present an invented variance threshold, retention period, phone number, completion service level, or escalation chain as existing company policy.","Do not claim that contractual lockup windows are legal deadlines or invent a legal difference between the two jurisdictions.","Do not let a security officer satisfy the two-person cash-count rule.","Do not authorise a stock or sales transaction as a cash-balancing mechanism."],"gold_validation":["Generate the gold DOCX offline and render it with a standard office library or LibreOffice.","Confirm the rendered document is no more than four total pages and remains readable at normal viewing size.","Recalculate every period comparison independently and confirm all figures satisfy the rubric tolerances.","Trace the normal path, both jurisdictional lone-closer paths, deferred-count completion, and the severe safety exception to coherent end states.","Confirm a newly authorised closer can use the procedure without needing a hidden contact, threshold, system instruction, or unwritten decision."],"intended_verdict":"A strong submission passes because it is an immediately usable, compact operating procedure that accurately normalizes the periods, preserves two-person cash accountability and the security deadline through a controlled deferral, separates stock and cash records, handles the severe safety event distinctly, and exposes unsupported local details for approval. A superficially polished submission should fail material items if it balances cash through shrink, uses the security officer as the second counter, tells a lone closer to keep recounting past lockup, invents policy thresholds, or attributes a cause unsupported by the figures."},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"mixed_media_bundle","structure":"required_sections"},"reference_files":[],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"closing_cash_control_procedure","filename":"bellwether_closing_cash_control_procedure.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"Presentation-ready operating procedure for normal closing, cash variances, lone-authorised-closer conditions, jurisdictional applicability, and the severe safety exception.","required":true,"constraints":["Place the file at the top level of the working directory using the exact filename.","The document must be editable and render correctly as a DOCX.","Maximum four pages total, with no appendices.","Write for a newly authorised Bellwether closing supervisor on their first unsupervised close.","Use only the supplied operating figures and clearly label unsupported company-specific details as assumptions for approval.","Do not include till-system click paths, opening procedures, bank-deposit transport, disciplinary investigation, staffing recommendations, or security-contract recommendations."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"plan_work","work_product":"operating_plan","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world_with_assumptions"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"retail_sales_supervisors","sector":"retail_trade","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":5.0,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"domain_expert","reviewer_policy":"The reference procedure should be drafted by an experienced retail cash-control supervisor and independently reviewed by one retail operations reviewer and one loss-prevention or internal-controls reviewer. Rendering and arithmetic must also be checked offline.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["No internal policy manual, contact directory, retention schedule, variance threshold, or system workflow is supplied; the gold must label any such proposed detail as an approval assumption.","The jurisdiction comparison concerns the supplied operating windows and site-specific emergency information, not a comprehensive statement of English or Scottish law.","The figures show a worsening pattern but cannot establish misconduct, root cause, or an effect of the security-provider transition."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T15:24:52+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T15:24:52+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T15:24:52+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T15:24:52+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_main/runs/3c90c9d469127b25","declared_deliverables":["bellwether_closing_cash_control_procedure.docx"]};
